James sought a more precise word to replace "reaches" in the sentence, "Under a scenario that reaches 2C by the end of the century, GDP impact stabilizes by mid-century." He highlighted that often temperatures peak above 2C and ideally wanted to convey a downward trend without delving into complexities. I suggested alternative words like "attains" or "approaches," resulting in revised sentences such as "Under a scenario that attains 2°C by the end of the century, GDP impact stabilizes by mid-century." This captures the intended meaning while avoiding misinterpretation of temperature trends.
